  "method": "124 components survived the sweep and fell into exactly thirty-one y-clusters, one per written name. Four were rejected by eye at magnification: the looping terminal of Cook on line 25, which crosses the first printed rule; two blots at the sheet's outer edge in the last free coloured column, where the footing row is blank; and a 12 px fragment standing on the closing rule. Every surviving mark was read a second time as a labelled montage of its own crop, and it is that second pass that says what each figure is. The free white female marks of this leaf sit 8 to 15 px above the free white male marks of the same line throughout, and that offset is what places line 31's lone female mark, which stands midway between two names."
