 "reconciliation": "ALL SIXTEEN columns this leaf carries a footing for close exactly, residual zero on every one - eight free white male and eight free white female. Nothing on this leaf is estimated, forced or left open. It is the cleanest hand of the group and its footings are what settle two forms of the enumerator's numeral alphabet against printed 214's: m_15_20 closes at 4 over a JOINED pair of diagonals, the same form printed 214's f_5_10 and f_40_50 carry, while printed 214's m_u5 closes at 11 over two SEPARATE diagonals - so the join, not the count of strokes, is what separates a 4 from a pair of 1s in this hand. m_5_10 here closes at 7 over a hooked glyph and f_15_20 closes at 7 over the same glyph, which is what reads it. THE FREE COLOURED BLOCK OF THIS LEAF IS EMPTY: no mark stands in any of its twelve columns and its twelve footings are blank, and the two components the sweep found at the sheet's outer edge are blots, not figures.",
